#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Declaring a labeler\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Labelers publish an `/app.bsky.labeler.service/self` record to declare that they are a labeler and publish their policies. That record looks like this:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "<LabelerServiceRecord />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you use [Ozone](/guides/using-ozone) as your labeler service, it will automatically publish this record for you when associating your account during the setup process.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `labelValues` declares what to expect from the Labeler. It may include global and custom label values.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `labelValueDefinitions` defines the custom labels. It includes the `locales` field for specifying human-readable copy in various languages. If the user's language is not found, it will use the first set of strings in the array.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "`subjectTypes`, `subjectCollections`, and `reasonTypes` declare what type of moderation reports are reviewed by the Labeler. `subjectTypes` can include `record` for individual pieces of content, and `account` for overall accounts. `subjectCollections` is a list of NSIDs of record types; if not defined, any record type is allowed. `reasonTypes` is a list of report reason codes (Lexicon references).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Updating your labeler\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Labeler service records created before support was added for new [`knownValues` in `reasonType`](https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto/blob/main/lexicons/com/atproto/moderation/defs.json) may need to be updated manually. Without an update, your labeler may receive reports with reason types it doesn't recognize — this is most likely to affect long-time maintainers who have added custom report reasons. You can check the [current `reasonType` definition](https://lexicon.garden/lexicon/did:plc:6msi3pj7krzih5qxqtryxlzw/com.atproto.moderation.defs#reasonType) to see if your record is out of date.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can update the record manually as you would [any other record](/guides/writing-data#updating-records). Alternatively, you can delete the `reasonType` field from your record entirely, which will cause your labeler to accept all report reason types, including any added in the future.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:31 src/guides/self-hosting/en.mdx:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Ozone\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Ozone](https://github.com/bluesky-social/ozone) is our reference labeling service for Atmosphere apps, and includes a web interface for triaging and actioning moderation reports.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Container>\n"
"  <Image src={ozone} alt=\"\" className=\"w-full max-w-md mx-auto\" />\n"
"</Container>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Self-hosting Ozone enables you to participate as a labeler in the AT stackable moderation architecture. The Ozone service consists of a web UI, a backend, and a Postgres database.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/creating-a-labeler/en.mdx:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before setting up your Ozone service you should create a *new* account on the network, separate from your main account. This is the account that subscribers to your labeler will interact with: accounts for labelers will appear differently in app interfaces than normal accounts. To get started with Ozone, read [Using Ozone](/guides/using-ozone).\n"
msgstr ""

